Rem ==================================================================
Rem halifax-core.shoddy — the calculator, with nothing that touches the
Rem world.
Rem
Rem Pure. Nothing here reads a file, writes one or prints: halifax.shoddy
Rem does all three and nothing else, and this half turns a typed line
Rem into the lines a shell should show. That is the whole reason for the
Rem split — a program with a prompt in it cannot be tested, and
Rem test.shoddy grades this file with no terminal anywhere near it.
Rem
Rem WHAT IS HERE AND WHAT IS NOT. Almost nothing of the calculator is in
Rem this file, and that is the point: the stack, the dictionary, the
Rem registers, the modes, UNDO, REDO, TRACE, the tape, HELP and WORDS are
Rem all reckoner's, and the arithmetic, statistics, money, matrices,
Rem files, clocks, randomness, CSV and boolean/bitwise words are the
Rem seed files'. What Halifax adds is an assembled state, a banner, and
Rem the words a shell has to answer for itself.
Rem
Rem THE WORDS THE SHELL OWNS. SAVE, LOAD and TAPESAVE name a path, QUIT
Rem and its second spelling EXIT end the session, and RESET builds a new
Rem state. None can be an ordinary dictionary word: the first three
Rem perform an effect and the engine performs none, QUIT/EXIT are the
Rem loop's business, and RESET has to know which seeds the dictionary was
Rem made from — which only this file does. They are intercepted from the
Rem line before it reaches RckEval.
Rem
Rem THEY ARE REGISTERED ANYWAY, for their metadata alone. The interception
Rem happens first so the registered body never runs in the real shell;
Rem what registration buys is that WORDS lists them and HELP SAVE
Rem answers. A mill whose file words are invisible to the two words
Rem someone explores with has hidden a third of itself.
Rem
Rem RENDERING IS NOT HERE EITHER. RckShow is the render, [ empty ] and
Rem [ depth n ] included, because the tape records the rendered rows and a
Rem second render in a mill would let the tape and the screen disagree.
Rem What this file owns are the lines AROUND the stack — the banner, the
Rem prompt, the tape pane — and each is a line-list producer so the
Rem full-screen face can reuse it unchanged.
Rem
Rem ---- THE MACHINES THAT ARE NOT SEEDED, AND WHY ----------------------
Rem
Rem Every machine in the tree with a seed is in the fold below. Ten are
Rem not, and this is the list, because "which seeds went into the last
Rem one" is a question only this file can answer and a reader deserves
Rem the whole answer rather than the half that is present.
Rem
Rem THEY ARE ALL THE SAME REFUSAL, and it is not that the work is
Rem outstanding. Each of these machines is a door onto a LIVE RESOURCE —
Rem a window, a socket, a sound device, the terminal itself, an open
Rem file handle — and R3.5(b) is why none of them can come to a prompt:
Rem a handle is a NUMBER capped at sixteen and shared across kinds, so
Rem an UNDO after opening one would restore the stack while leaving the
Rem resource open and now unreachable. That is not a guard that can be
Rem written more carefully. It is the shape of the thing.
Rem
Rem   isam     — a table, and a record layout. This is the one worth
Rem              spelling out, because it looks the most nearly possible
Rem              and is in fact the least: seedisam.shoddy exists and
Rem              works, but RckSeedIsamNum takes an ALREADY-OPEN handle
Rem              AND a cellOf function, and an ISAM file's record layout
Rem              is reader/writer/key functions written in Shoddy and
Rem              compiled in. A host program has those. A calculator
Rem              cannot be told a record layout at a prompt, and no
Rem              amount of guarding changes that — so halifax has no
Rem              source for a table, and never will have one it did not
Rem              have compiled into it.
Rem   recio    — binary records over BOpen, the same handle again, and
Rem              the reason seedneural.shoddy bridges the TEXT weight
Rem              file and not the binary one.
Rem   turtle,
Rem   scribbler,
Rem   plotter  — a drawing surface. There is no window here; there is a
Rem              prompt.
Rem   buzzer   — a sound device, likewise.
Rem   vt100    — the terminal, which this shell already owns. Two things
Rem              driving one screen is one thing driving it wrongly.
Rem   keys     — raw keystrokes, which InputLine already owns, for the
Rem              same reason.
Rem   net,
Rem   https    — sockets, and a gated capability besides: they need the
Rem              mill run with --allow-net, which a calculator asking for
Rem              the network mid-session cannot obtain.
Rem
Rem WHAT WOULD CHANGE THIS is not a better seed. It is a resource the
Rem ENGINE could name without putting a handle on the stack — a table or
Rem a socket held by the state and referred to by name, opened and closed
Rem by the shell rather than by a word. That is a design, and it is not
Rem this one; recording it as absent is the honest alternative to leaving
Rem ten machines looking merely forgotten.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "../../machines/seq.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/reckoner.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedmath.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedstats.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedseq.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedstr.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedmoney.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedmatrix.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seeddict.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedfile.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedclock.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedrandom.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedcsv.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedbool.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedshaker.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedjson.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedxml.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedhtml.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedsimplex.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedlin.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedeng.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedfin.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedalg.shoddy"
Include "../../machines/seeds/seedneural.shoddy"

Rem ---- what a typed line turns out to be -------------------------------

Rem The shell reads one of these and does one thing per case. A line the
Rem shell has no business in is HxEval and goes to the engine whole,
Rem including a line that will not even tokenize: the engine's refusal for
Rem an unterminated string is the one everyone should see, and a second
Rem tokenizer here would be a second answer to the same question.
Type HxAsk = HxEval(AskLine As String) | HxPath(PathWord As String, PathName As String) | HxPlain(PlainWord As String) | HxAskBad(AskWhy As String)

Def HxSaveWord() As String
    "SAVE"

Def HxLoadWord() As String
    "LOAD"

Def HxTapeSaveWord() As String
    "TAPESAVE"

Def HxQuitWord() As String
    "QUIT"

Rem A second spelling of QUIT and nothing more — same interception, same
Rem refusal if it turns up mid-line, same HELP text. Kept as its own
Rem word rather than folded into HxQuitWord so QUIT itself, and what it
Rem does, is untouched.
Def HxExitWord() As String
    "EXIT"

Def HxResetWord() As String
    "RESET"

Rem The three that name a file, and the three that name nothing.
Def HxPathWords() As List Of String
    { HxSaveWord(), HxLoadWord(), HxTapeSaveWord() }

Def HxPlainWords() As List Of String
    { HxQuitWord(), HxExitWord(), HxResetWord() }

Def HxShellWordNames() As List Of String
    Concat(HxPathWords(), HxPlainWords())

Rem A shell word is only a shell word as the WHOLE line. Anywhere else in
Rem a line it is an ordinary token and the engine refuses it through the
Rem registered stub, which is why 3 4 SAVE "x" says so rather than quietly
Rem writing a file in the middle of a calculation.
Def HxRead(line As String) As HxAsk
    Select Case RckTokens(line)
        Case Ok(toks)
            HxReadToks(line, toks)
        Case Else
            HxEval(line)

Def HxReadToks(line As String, toks As List Of String) As HxAsk
    If IsEmpty(toks) Then
        HxEval(line)
    Else
        HxReadFirst(line, Upper(First(toks)), Rest(toks))

Def HxReadFirst(line As String, head As String, more As List Of String) As HxAsk
    If Contains(HxPathWords(), head) Then
        HxReadPath(head, more)
    Else
        If Contains(HxPlainWords(), head) Then
            HxReadPlain(head, more)
        Else
            HxEval(line)

Rem The path is a quoted string, as it is everywhere else in the language.
Rem An unquoted word would read as a dictionary name and a bare path with
Rem a space in it would read as two tokens, so the quotes are the whole of
Rem the grammar rather than a decoration on it.
Def HxReadPath(head As String, more As List Of String) As HxAsk
    If IsEmpty(more) Then
        HxAskBad(head & " needs a file name in quotes after it")
    Else
        If Not RckIsText(First(more)) Then
            HxAskBad(head & " needs its file name in quotes, not " & First(more))
        Else
            HxReadPathEnd(head, RckTextOf(First(more)), Rest(more))

Def HxReadPathEnd(head As String, name As String, rest As List Of String) As HxAsk
    If Not IsEmpty(rest) Then
        HxAskBad(head & " takes one file name and nothing after it")
    Else
        If name = "" Then
            HxAskBad(head & " needs a file name, and the quotes are empty")
        Else
            HxPath(head, name)

Def HxReadPlain(head As String, more As List Of String) As HxAsk
    If IsEmpty(more) Then
        HxPlain(head)
    Else
        HxAskBad(head & " takes nothing after it")

Rem Whether a line is QUIT and nothing else. The shell's loop has to know
Rem this BEFORE it takes its turn, because the loop is one self-recursive
Rem Def and a turn that could end the session would have to hand back a
Rem stop for some other Def to act on — which would make the tail call a
Rem mutual one and put a frame on the stack per line entered. So the test
Rem is pure, it lives here with the rest of the reading, and QUIT 5 is not
Rem a quit: it goes to the turn and earns a refusal like any other line
Rem with something wrong in it.
Def HxQuits(line As String) As Boolean
    Select Case HxRead(line)
        Case HxPlain(w)
            w = HxQuitWord() Or w = HxExitWord()
        Case Else
            False

Rem ---- the state a session starts from ---------------------------------

Rem The seven seeds of R1.1, then the five that followed, in order, and
Rem then the shell's own five. The order is the order WORDS groups them
Rem in, which is the order someone built the dictionary in and the order
Rem they will look for a word in.
Def HxFresh() As RckState
    Let s1 = RckSeedMath(RckNew())
    Let s2 = RckSeedStats(s1)
    Let s3 = RckSeedSeq(s2)
    Let s4 = RckSeedStr(s3)
    Let s5 = RckSeedMoney(s4)
    Let s6 = RckSeedMatrix(s5)
    Let s7 = RckSeedDict(s6)
    Let s8 = RckSeedFile(s7)
    Let s9 = RckSeedClock(s8)
    Let s10 = RckSeedRandom(s9)
    Let s11 = RckSeedCsv(s10)
    Let s12 = RckSeedBool(s11)
    Let s13 = RckSeedShaker(s12)
    Let s14 = RckSeedJson(s13)
    Let s15 = RckSeedXml(s14)
    Let s16 = RckSeedHtml(s15)
    Let s17 = RckSeedSimplex(s16)
    Let s18 = RckSeedLin(s17)
    Let s19 = RckSeedEng(s18)
    Let s20 = RckSeedFin(s19)
    Let s21 = RckSeedAlg(s20)
    Let s22 = RckSeedNeural(s21)
    HxShellSeed(s22)

Def HxShellName() As String
    "shell"

Rem Registered for HELP and WORDS. The bodies are refusals because a body
Rem that ran would mean the interception had failed, and a refusal is what
Rem the engine answers with everywhere else. The three file words and QUIT
Rem are RckTouch so WORDS groups them under "touches the world" — which is
Rem true of them, whoever ends up carrying it out; RESET is RckPure,
Rem because building a fresh dictionary touches nothing.
Def HxShellSeed(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s0 = RckSeeding(st, HxShellName())
    Let s1 = RckReg(s0, HxSaveWord(), 0, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => HxShellOnly(HxSaveWord())), "( -- )", "Write the words you have defined to a file: SAVE " & RckQuoteMark() & "mine.halifax" & RckQuoteMark() & ".")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, HxLoadWord(), 0, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => HxShellOnly(HxLoadWord())), "( -- )", "Read a file of definitions back in; one bad line refuses the whole file.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, HxTapeSaveWord(), 0, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => HxShellOnly(HxTapeSaveWord())), "( -- )", "Write the tape to a file, exactly as it was shown.")
    Let s4 = RckReg(s3, HxQuitWord(), 0, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => HxShellOnly(HxQuitWord())), "( -- )", "Leave. Nothing is saved for you; SAVE first if you want your words kept.")
    Let s5 = RckReg(s4, HxExitWord(), 0, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => HxShellOnly(HxExitWord())), "( -- )", "Leave, exactly like QUIT. Nothing is saved for you; SAVE first if you want your words kept.")
    Let s6 = RckReg(s5, HxResetWord(), 0, RckPure(Fn(vs) => HxShellOnly(HxResetWord())), "( -- )", "Start again: empty stack, no history, no tape, and only the words you started with.")
    RckSeeding(s6, RckUserName())

Def HxShellOnly(name As String) As RckWork
    RckWorkBad(name & " is the shell's word, not the dictionary's: type it as the whole line and nothing else")

Rem ---- what the shell shows -------------------------------------------

Def HxBanner() As List Of String
    { "shoddy halifax — RPN. Numbers go on the stack; words work on them.",
      "WORDS lists, HELP <word> explains, TRACE follows, UNDO backs out, QUIT (or EXIT) leaves." }

Rem The prompt IS the tape's mark, deliberately: a tape row is the prompt
Rem with what was typed after it, so a saved tape reads back as the
Rem session it was.
Def HxPrompt() As String
    RckTapeMark()

Rem A transaction: the lines to show, and the state to carry on from. Both
Rem cases of RckLine are covered here and nowhere else, so the shell never
Rem matches on an engine type.
Def HxShown(r As RckLine) As List Of String
    Select Case r
        Case RckNext(st, out)
            Concat(out, RckShow(st))
        Case RckStop(st, why, out)
            Concat(Append(out, RckWhyMark() & why), RckShow(st))
        Case Else
            { RckWhyMark() & "the line did not answer" }

Def HxAfter(st As RckState, r As RckLine) As RckState
    Select Case r
        Case RckNext(st2, out)
            st2
        Case RckStop(st2, why, out)
            st2
        Case Else
            st

Rem One typed line, evaluated. This is what the shell loops on and what
Rem the test drives; the shell adds a prompt and a Print and nothing else.
Def HxDo(st As RckState, line As String) As RckLine
    RckEval(st, line)

Rem A refusal the shell itself raises — a bad SAVE line, a file that is
Rem not there — shown the same way the engine's are, and recorded on the
Rem tape the same way, because to the person reading it there is no
Rem difference between the two.
Def HxRefused(st As RckState, line As String, why As String) As RckLine
    RckStop(RckTapedBad(st, line, { }, why), why, { })

Rem And a confirmation, for the same reason: "saved 1 word" belongs on the
Rem tape between the line that caused it and the stack that followed.
Def HxSaid(st As RckState, line As String, said As String) As RckLine
    RckNext(RckTapedOk(st, st, line, { said }), { said })

Rem ---- the tape pane ---------------------------------------------------

Rem The last n rows, oldest first, for a pane that is shorter than the
Rem tape. Asking for more rows than there are is not an error: a session
Rem three lines old fills three lines of the pane and leaves the rest.
Def HxTapePane(st As RckState, n As Number) As List Of String
    HxLastRows(RckTape(st), n)

Def HxLastRows(rows As List Of String, n As Number) As List Of String
    If n < 1 Then
        { }
    Else
        If Length(rows) <= n Then
            rows
        Else
            DropN(rows, Length(rows) - n)

Rem ---- counting, for the shell's confirmations ------------------------

Def HxUserCount(st As RckState) As Number
    Length(Filter(RckDict(st), RckIsUser))

Rem "1 word", "2 words" — the English, in one place, because it is needed
Rem for words and for rows and getting it wrong twice would be worse than
Rem getting it wrong once.
Def HxCounted(n As Number, one As String, many As String) As String
    If n = 1 Then
        Str(n) & " " & one
    Else
        Str(n) & " " & many
